{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991798-looking-for-tips-on-gming-to-give-players-more-freedom","id":991798,"title":"Looking for Tips on GMing to give players more freedom.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T04:07:58-07:00","id":991798,"title":"Looking for Tips on GMing to give players more freedom.","content":"So I've been running a vampire/changeling game for a bit and its been alot of fun I thought for everyone but the players feel like they don't have any freedom. I thought they did and based on what happened or what they did I would have the world react. I thought they would follow what was going on because they wanted to not because they felt obligated but from last night's game I can clearly see they still don't think they have any freedom so now I feel depressed I sucked the fun out the game for them in some way. <br /> <br /> So any tips on putting together stories that give players more freedom to do what they want with their characters ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:50:52-07:00","id":991830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991798-looking-for-tips-on-gming-to-give-players-more-freedom#post991798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So any tips on putting together stories that give players more freedom to do what they want with their characters ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read and let them fulfill their Aspirations? They should be at least players ways of taking route on running the plot by the,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:59:14-07:00","id":991852,"title":"","content":"Don't beat yourself up. These kind of things happen. <br /> <br /> Aspirations are a good place to start, they don't have to just be goals of the character but the player as well and that level of meta control gives them agency. Agency they can use to inform what they want out of the game.<br /> <br /> If you have a metaplot going, I've found it helps to ease off it a little and let players indulge in world building. Gathering allies, contacts, or getting into hijinx. <br /> <br /> Ex. My players were investigating the poisoning of an affluent heiress which led them to a gang they were suppose to only have a brief interaction with, because of their free will it turned into a lengthy multi session war with these smugglers, resulting in the gangs complete dissolvement. Cool stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10827-baronzobops","name":"baronzobops","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10827_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:51:58-07:00","id":991907,"title":"","content":"Wyrdhamster's got it. Base the game around their aspirations. Have their actions result in consequences that advance the plot. Unless they're part of a faction or have chosen to do something that gives them a 'line of command' like an Invictus sworn to follow their sire, don't have people order them what to do, and even then don't force them to do it. Don't warn them away from their choices unless it's a matter of miscommunication, in which case you should just clarify and let them decide.<br /> <br /> What have you been doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:46:12-07:00","id":991960,"title":"","content":"Aspirations are a thing, as are any other way to just ask the players to wright down what they want, like a Background. Just don't make it into another obligation.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, when you ask the players what they're going to do next, just ask what they <u>want</u> to do. Point out that they have options, even options you maybe aren't yourself aware. And point out that the NPCs don't have guns pointed to their heads right now, and never if they're not caught. Players can misunderstand NPCs' requests for the only possibilities, and you can dissolve the feeling just pointing out that it isn't that way.<br /> <br /> From that, we need to know the specifics of your game and your way of running it to say something more, but don't feel so low. Running a game isn't easy, but in the end what counts is to have fun, and if your players are going to the next session, so they're probably having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}